\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. At Thy feet, O Christ, we lay
\par Thine own gift of this new day;
\par Doubt of what  it holds in store
\par Makes us crave Thine aid the more;
\par Lest it prove a time of loss,
\par Mark it, Saviour, with Thy Cross.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. If it flow on calm and bright,
\par Be Thyself our chief delight;
\par If it bring unknown distress,
\par Good is all that Thou canst bless;
\par Only, while its hours begin,
\par Pray we, keep them clear of sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We in part our weakness know,
\par And in part discern our foe;
\par Well for us, before Thine eyes
\par All our danger open lies;
\par Turn not from us while we plead
\par Thy compassions and our need.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fain would we Thy word embrace,
\par Live each moment in Thy grace,
\par All ourselves to Thee consign,
\par Fold up all our wills in Thine,
\par Think, and speak, and do, and be
\par Simply that which pleases Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hear us, Lord, and that right soon;
\par Hear, and grant the choicest boon
\par That Thy love can e'er impart,
\par Loyal singleness of heart;
\par So shall this and all our days,
\par Christ our God, show forth Thy praise. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

